    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d803">

                <pb facs="0731" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg647"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114A/219</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-17T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 17, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3137. For Dresel [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 144. Replying Legation’s 5057, October 5, 3 p.m., your 205. Board sustains
                    action of A[llied] B[lockade] C[ommittee] in Paris [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Berne</hi>] of refusing shipments for Y.M.C.A. into Germany for the use of
                    Russians who were once prisoners but are now held there in duress.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
